From: DBY-W09 contributors <dby-w09@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: qcom-spmi-adc5: expose 30K battery thermistor voltage

Expose the PM8150B battery thermistor channel with a 30K pull-up as
processed voltage for DBY-W09. Thermistor characteristics are board
specific; do not apply the existing 100K thermistor temperature table.
Reuse the standard ADC5 conversion and voltage scaling paths unchanged.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
Signed-off-by: DBY-W09 contributors <dby-w09@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5.c
@@ -542,6 +542,8 @@
 					SCALE_HW_CALIB_DEFAULT)
 	[ADC5_XO_THERM_100K_PU]	= ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("xo_therm", 0,
 					SCALE_HW_CALIB_XOTHERM)
+	[ADC5_BAT_THERM_30K_PU]	= ADC5_CHAN_VOLT("bat_therm_30k", 0,
+					SCALE_HW_CALIB_DEFAULT)
 	[ADC5_BAT_ID_100K_PU]	= ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("bat_id", 0,
 					SCALE_HW_CALIB_DEFAULT)
 	[ADC5_AMUX_THM1_100K_PU] = ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("amux_thm1_100k_pu", 0,
